  "worked_solution": "Any vector from $\\text{Im}(T)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2z \\\\ w \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]=z{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{{v}_{1}}+w{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{{v}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $\\text{Im}(T)=\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}.$ Therefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=2.$ \n\nFinally, according the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T) & =4-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
